 "differences": [
  "The published numbers used for checking are those of the authors' preprint (PsyArXiv 56zwg, 2023); the journal version (Cognition 2025) could not be read here and may differ.",
  "Three preprint values are the computed ones cut rather than rounded, so they are not used as checks: Experiment 1 English sentence F1 change mean 17.956 (printed 17.95), Experiment 1 English transfer F1 SD 20.976 (printed 20.97), Experiment 2 English sentence F2 change mean 20.577 (printed 20.57).",
  "Sex: the files give 14 women and 1 man in Experiment 4 and 12 women and 3 men in Experiment 5; the preprint text says 13 and 2 in each (60 women and 15 men in all five experiments, which the files reproduce). The mean age in the files is 22.48 years (preprint: 22.89), so one or two files may be assigned to a different experiment, or ages differ.",
  "Seven participants have no S1 (first baseline) data: the arrays hold zeros for the whole block, which are emptied here (S1 is used only in Experiment 5's new-sentence after-effect measure)."
 ],
